WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.669
Let's consult a map.

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:04.337
Here's Germany.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.880
Morocco.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.549
And Fantasyland.

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:12.762
But beyond Walt Disney World's borders

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:14.514
you find a larger boundary.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.976
The Central Florida Tourism Oversight District

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:20.103
that's been at the center of a feud

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:22.564
between Disney and Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:24.899
“There's a new sheriff in town.”

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:28.695
But this district started way before 
the DeSantis-Disney war.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.365
It explains something about the history of Florida...

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:34.117
and the lost city of EPCOT.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.662
“It will be a community of tomorrow
that will never be completed.”

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:42.000
And most importantly, 
why Disney World is here...

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:45.086
and isn't moving anytime soon.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.883
This isn't Disney World, 
but Disneyland.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.635
And the key thing is not the park

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:54.763
but the surroundings.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.765
Downtown Anaheim.

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:59.476
A 40 minute drive from Los Angeles.

00:01:01.936 --> 00:01:04.355
Disneyland opened in 1955.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.776
In an internal publication, Disney
showed its belief

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:12.197
that the site provided sufficient land 
for present and future growth.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.450
Period photos show the area didn't start

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.452
as densely developed as it is today,.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:21.873
But this 1965 map shows how quickly 
things changed.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:25.001
Everything from schools 
to shopping centers

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:27.837
limited Disneyland's control over its future.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.799
Walt Disney needed more...

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.801
and he wanted to get more 

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:33.885
from a new park.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.309
He wanted his new park to be 
on the East Coast.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:45.647
He needed a lot of land, so dense 
urban areas were out.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.232
He didn't want cold.

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:49.484
That narrowed things down to Florida.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:51.778
He also didn't want to compete 
with the ocean

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.322
so he skipped coastal locations.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:02:00.120
When flying over Orlando, he saw I-4, 
I-95, and the Sunshine State Parkway.

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:01.538
That clinched it.

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:04.374
Locals started to notice 
big land deals

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.376
being made by mystery companies.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:11.047
Soon, Floridians began to suspect 
their mystery industry was Disney.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.261
The size was immense.

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:19.305
Here's the size of Disneyland
if it were in Florida.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.141
And here is the land

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.977
they bought for Disney World as it is today.

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:26.771
Even after some land was sold off.

00:02:26.896 --> 00:02:28.773
Shortly after the land story broke

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:31.860
Disney held a press conference 
with Governor Hayden Burns 

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.946
and brother Roy Disney 
to discuss the plans.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.783
“It will bring a new world of entertainment...

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.996
pleasure, and economic development 
to the state of Florida.”

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:43.788
“Walt Disney.”

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:46.124
Let's break down this next Walt Disney quote.

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:49.419
After you've done something you see

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:52.547
with the experience and all of that,

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:54.674
what you might do if you were starting from scratch.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:58.511
Disney wanted to get right 
what he missed in Anaheim.

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:00.638
“Taking a look at the land this morning

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:02.724
I say we are starting from scratch.”

00:03:03.766 --> 00:03:06.853
The land needed a lot of work, 
drainage work, development:

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:07.395
everything.

00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:10.064
Just look at this 1962 map of the area.

00:03:10.773 --> 00:03:12.609
There were some orange groves 
on the land

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:14.736
but this symbol means swamp.

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:17.697
The area is called the Reedy Creek Swamp.

00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:20.450
“But we have many things in mind

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.411
that would make this unique and different
from Disneyland.”

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:25.246
But Disney also had greater ambitions

00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:28.291
for the land that he would 
only reveal later on.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.211
“Here in Florida

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.796
we have something special we've never 
enjoyed at Disney.”

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.257
“There's enough land here to hold

00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:39.052
all the ideas and plans we could possibly imagine.”

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:42.347
To persuade Florida's government 
to support the project...

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:45.099
Disney released concept art like this...

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.560
that showed way more than a theme park.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.896
Like a giant industrial complex.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.148
And a constantly evolving city

00:03:52.148 --> 00:03:54.359
of 30,000 people.

00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:59.322
EPCOT: An Experimental Prototype Community 
of Tomorrow.

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:02.617
“All these varied activities around the Disney World...

00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:06.955
will be tied together by a high speed, 
rapid transit system

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:09.707
running almost the full length 
of the property.”

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.794
“It will never cease to be a living 
blueprint of the future...

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:15.546
where people actually live a life

00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:17.715
they can't find anywhere else 
in the world.”

00:04:17.715 --> 00:04:22.095
But Disney didn't want to wait for permits 
for every sewer drain and light post

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.179
in his city of tomorrow.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.848
To have complete dominion 
over the land he'd bought...

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.977
he needed political control, 
not just a title.

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:31.271
He needed a kingdom.

00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:34.065
Special districts are common.

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:37.402
Tens of thousands of them exist 
across the United States.

00:04:38.236 --> 00:04:41.447
For example, the famous retirement community,
The Villages

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.491
just north of Disney 
uses them.

00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:45.576
These let residents vote on a board

00:04:45.576 --> 00:04:48.579
which then establishes policies 
that can raise taxes,

00:04:48.579 --> 00:04:51.416
build stuff, or fund public safety 
departments.

00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:54.794
This can happen across municipal 
boundaries, county lines...

00:04:55.086 --> 00:04:57.297
or other traditional boundaries.

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:59.841
Disney wanted a superpowered version of this...

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:03.886
with Disney staff as the sole voting 
"residents" inside it.

00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:05.972
They would be able to vote themselves in

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.890
and make their own rules.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.477
The Disney World land is split

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.063
between Orange and Osceola Counties.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.482
It also includes what planning documents list

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.985
as jurisdictions of the city of Bay Lake

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:22.989
unincorporated areas and the city 
of Lake Buena Vista

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.824
all of which were created for

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.993
and are largely controlled 
by Disney.

00:05:27.118 --> 00:05:29.746
They had multiple points of leverage 
to get this.

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:32.165
“I believe we can build a community

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.376
that more people will talk about 
and come to look at...

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.296
than any other area in the world.”

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:41.257
All these plans meant promise of 
economic development

00:05:41.257 --> 00:05:43.301
for a relatively sleepy area.

00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:47.138
“I predict that we'll experience 
at least a 50%...

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:52.018
and possibly a 100% increase in tourism
in the state of Florida.”

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:55.229
Disney could also threaten 
to pursue alternate sites...

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:58.149
in northern California in Mineral King.

00:05:58.441 --> 00:06:01.194
They had a parallel proposal
to build a ski complex

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:04.155
that was closer to Anaheim 
and less swampy.

00:06:04.238 --> 00:06:06.783
It ended up serving as a taunt to Florida.

00:06:06.824 --> 00:06:08.326
The result was clear. 

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:10.953
In the same issue of Disney's
internal magazine

00:06:10.953 --> 00:06:11.954
in which they announced

00:06:11.954 --> 00:06:13.831
the biggest surprise of the decade

00:06:13.831 --> 00:06:16.376
Florida's VIPs were already flying out...

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:19.170
to begin working on project problems.

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:22.715
Other places didn't grant big powers 
like Florida.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.009
There was no ski resort 
in Mineral King

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:26.803
because the Sierra Club fought it

00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:29.097
and the state never approved it.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:32.266
All that is why Disney World 
is here.

00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:36.979
In May 1967, the Reedy Creek 
Improvement District 

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:40.858
was chartered as an entity that could 
regulate across counties..

00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:42.193
like its own government.

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:45.905
It could control sewage, generation of power
by nuclear fission

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:49.075
airport facilities, railroads, 
and construction.

00:06:49.117 --> 00:06:51.244
And Disney used its powers.

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:54.330
The company created an 
underground tunnel system

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.541
for their utilities 
called utilidors.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:07:01.337
Each tunnel had spots for ventilation, water
and transportation.

00:07:01.546 --> 00:07:04.507
They built the monorail and they created 
their own lake.

00:07:04.882 --> 00:07:06.551
The Seven Seas Lagoon.

00:07:06.551 --> 00:07:09.262
So the parking lot wouldn't sit too close to the castle.

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:11.055
They did it all because... 

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:12.348
they could. 

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:16.394
In 1966, Walt Disney died 
in Los Angeles.

00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:20.022
The city part of his Disney World dream 
mostly died with him

00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:21.941
despite some gestures toward building it.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:25.528
EPCOT became a part of the theme park 
in 1982...

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:26.946
but it was not a city.

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:29.532
The district's comprehensive 10-year-plan shows

00:07:29.532 --> 00:07:32.702
how far the Disney dream has drifted 
from EPCOT.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.122
Undeveloped land is labeled green 
for conservation

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:38.875
not as the foundation for some future city.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.295
Mass transportation consists of busses 
and the monorail line

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:45.006
rather than the intricate transit network

00:07:45.006 --> 00:07:46.382
that Disney envisioned.

00:07:46.382 --> 00:07:50.178
Disney has massive populations 
staying in its many hotels

00:07:50.178 --> 00:07:54.849
but when you look at a map of permanent 
residential addresses in the district

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:57.310
you see 8 here and 9 here.

00:07:57.351 --> 00:08:00.938
It's projected to be about 
43 people by 2027.

00:08:01.856 --> 00:08:05.860
Disney ensured that later residential developments 
didn't change things.

00:08:06.027 --> 00:08:10.156
Development of Disney's "imagineered" small town 
Celebration, Florida...

00:08:10.531 --> 00:08:12.742
began on the district in the 1990s

00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:15.286
but it was de-annexed from Reedy Creek.

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:19.040
The same happened for the Disney-owned
Plantation Park Condos

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.166
in Little Lake Bryan.

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:23.503
Being cut out of the district means 
no voting for the board.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:26.088
All of this was just background...

00:08:26.547 --> 00:08:28.049
until the feud.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:33.679
“Welcome to the Walt Disney Company's 
annual meeting of shareholders.”

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.307
“I called Governor DeSantis this morning

00:08:36.307 --> 00:08:38.601
to express our disappointment and concern.”

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:42.688
Disney's CEO called to protest Florida's
"Don’t Say Gay" law

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.815
which restricts classroom instruction

00:08:44.815 --> 00:08:47.026
about sexual orientation.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:52.365
“We believe being joined at the hip 
with this one California-based company

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:56.118
was not something that was 
justifiable or sustainable”

00:08:56.285 --> 00:08:57.161
And promised...

00:08:57.161 --> 00:09:00.289
“The corporate kingdom finally 
comes to an end.”

00:09:00.289 --> 00:09:02.083
But the taunting continued.

00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:05.920
“Second Quarter 2023 Financial Results 
Conference Call.”

00:09:05.962 --> 00:09:08.172
“So this is plainly a matter of retaliation

00:09:08.172 --> 00:09:10.758
while the rest of the Florida 
special districts

00:09:10.758 --> 00:09:13.135
continue operating basically 
as they were.”

00:09:13.344 --> 00:09:16.305
“Someone even said, like, maybe you need 
another state prison.”

00:09:16.305 --> 00:09:16.931
“Who knows?”

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:20.768
“I mean, I just think that 
the possibilities are endless.”

00:09:20.977 --> 00:09:22.812
Still, the state would struggle

00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:25.356
to actually dissolve the district.

00:09:25.606 --> 00:09:28.776
The charter gives the district
the power to finance the projects

00:09:28.776 --> 00:09:31.362
and activities of the district 
through bonds.

00:09:31.696 --> 00:09:35.408
If the district disappeared, hundreds 
of millions in bond debt

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:39.745
would probably flow to taxpayers in 
Orange and Osceola Counties.

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:41.789
And on the other side,

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:47.128
Disney has already made noise about 
a $17 billion Disney World expansion.

00:09:47.378 --> 00:09:50.548
In the end, Disney's district has had 
a name change

00:09:50.548 --> 00:09:54.176
and board composition and process 
may slightly change.

00:09:54.635 --> 00:09:58.222
But Germany and Morocco 
aren't going anywhere.

00:09:58.806 --> 00:10:02.393
The kingdom will probably stay 
a kingdom.

